WEBVTT

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.000
Five, four...

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.040
Three, two...

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.250
One, zero.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.460
It's taking you too long
to line the pins up with the shear line.

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:16.420
I'm sorry I have to keep asking you
to help me with this, Miss Dorothy.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.330
Oh, it's not your fault.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.130
I mean, the other options...

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:23.670
Watch.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:24.830
All right.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
Um, how did you do that?

00:00:31.790 --> 00:00:33.130
Watch closely.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:35.540
See?

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.500
No, I, um...

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.830
There. Now you try.

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:50.290
They're just not cut out to be teachers.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:55.170
I believe they are saying rude things about us.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.080
I think it's fair to get angry.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.540
Maybe we should go with something simpler.

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.040
You really like that song, don't you, Miss Dorothy?

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.790
Was I singing?

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.460
Yes! You hum that tune all the time.

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:14.790
Do I?

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.290
Not him, either.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.540
The Kingdom Foreign Office's cipher?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.500
Yes. It's been planted inside the liaison's body.

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.170
Inside the body? And you want me
to grab the liaison and remove the cipher?

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.750
He's already dead.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.790
He should be taken to the morgue in the next few days.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.500
You want me to raid a corpse.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.670
It's better than killing, I'd say.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:28.040
Numbers one and two
on my list of least favorite spy jobs.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.380
What's the target's name?

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:31.920
We don't know.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:35.710
Don't tell me you want me to clean out
every corpse in the morgue?

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:38.580
The Duke of Normandy has an accomplice there.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.630
He knows who to look for.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.880
I'm supposed to be working Operation: Changeling.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.080
Why did you choose me?

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.540
Because that accomplice is someone
with whom you are well acquainted.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.380
Danny MacBean.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.540
Your father.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:11.920
Oh, it was just a cat.

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:15.000
Sorry to drag you along for this.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.540
Not at all.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:20.210
If anything happens, I'll need someone to act as liaison.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.630
Of course.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:24.880
But what IS this place?

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.460
We call it Ghost Street.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:31.880
They say half the people
who go down this road never come back.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.210
Half?

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:34.920
Why is that?

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.170
Because it leads to the morgue.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.380
We're always shorthanded here.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.210
I'll have you get right to work.

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:51.290
Yes, Ma'am.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.250
The work is nothing too complicated.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:59.580
When the bodies come in,
you remove their clothing and wipe them clean.

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:03.250
Then you look for anything that might identify them.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.500
If no one comes to claim them,

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.830
we put them on the carriage to the graveyard.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:11.080
Every day it's more of the same.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.290
Damn you, you were laughing at me!

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.250
No, I was...

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.540
That's right! It wasn't about you!

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:19.920
Defending her, are you?

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.500
I bet you two are friends in bed, too!

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.750
You're joining giblets, ain't ya?

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.000
We are not!

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.710
That's quite enough, Danny!

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.420
No, I can tell! The bitch and the studhorse!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:35.750
For goodness' sake, not him again.

00:05:36.250 --> 00:05:38.380
He's as low as they come, isn't he?

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.580
Er, um...

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.630
Daisy!

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.250
Daisy, is that you?!

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:50.170
Too stubborn to pop off, eh?

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.460
That's my girl!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.420
Yeah. It's been a while, hasn't it, Dad?

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.210
Oh, my. The morgue?

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.880
Yes, dead bodies from all over London end up there.

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.000
I didn't know so many people died every day.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:13.540
Oh.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.540
And Control is so awful.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:18.040
They know about Miss Dorothy's situation,

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:20.380
yet they're making her spend time
with that horrible father.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.330
Father?

00:06:22.580 --> 00:06:23.790
N-never mind.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.420
Wh-what tea would you like to have tonight?

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:30.000
How about Uva? Or would you prefer Keemun?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:43.880
And what brings you here, Young Lady?

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:44.710
Eh?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:47.880
Is it debt? Or are you an immigrant?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.170
Um, well...

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.380
Oh, you don't have to tell me if you don't want to.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.380
Everyone here has their reasons.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.040
This place is largely ignored by the rest of the world.

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:01.880
And that's exactly what some of us want.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:05.000
Even you, Sir?

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:10.000
My leg was ruined in the War.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.670
I killed too many people.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.040
And all my friends are gone.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.460
Maybe that's why.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.420
I feel right at home working with the dead.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.880
If we steal the cipher, then Dad will...

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.460
Why? Of all the possible...

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:35.130
My luck is changing, I swear.

00:07:35.290 --> 00:07:38.130
You want me to pay back what I owe, don't ya?

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.830
I'm a lot of things, but I ain't a liar.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:44.290
Just taking a bit longer than planned, is all.

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.000
So...

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.830
You still have work to do.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.630
I'm taking a break, Love.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.750
Danny.

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:53.330
Who is this woman?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.040
My daughter, Daisy.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:58.500
By pure coincidence,
she came to work with me just the other day.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.750
Ooh, a touching reunion.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.290
A looker like you must have any number of men
dying for your hand.

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.960
I want to earn my own money.

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:13.170
I'd be up the creek if my future husband
ended up like my dad.

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:16.710
Daisy! What do you know about anything?!

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.710
It's true, isn't it?!

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:23.880
There are plenty of people out who've gotten hurt
and are still doing what they can!

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:27.170
You're just using your injury as an excuse to run away!

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:29.670
Daisy!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:30.630
Wait, Daisy!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.380
Ah-ah-ah. Our discussion isn't over.

00:08:35.000 --> 00:08:36.000
Miss Dorothy-

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.670
Well, you should listen to your daughter and get to work.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.830
I didn't lose my hand 'cause I wanted to!

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:50.330
Damn it all to Hell!

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.750
Damn you all!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:54.460
Little brat ain't lived half as long as I have!
What does she know?!

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:57.250
She's got no idea how much I've... how much I've...!

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.380
Please stop it!

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.630
You should be ashamed of yourself!

00:09:01.750 --> 00:09:03.710
Taking your anger out on everything around you!

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.290
Who the Hell are you?

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:08.960
You're her father, aren't you?

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:12.250
Then maybe you should start to act like it, Sir!

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.670
What did you say, you little brat?

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.130
What's this thingamajig?

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:23.920
Please don't do that!

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.290
You're an interesting little girl.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.420
No, stop!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.080
Stop that!

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:32.170
Huh?

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:36.880
Daisy...!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.580
Are you all right, Beatrice?

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:40.460
Y-yes.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:44.250
A-a friend of yours, is she?

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.500
We... we were just having a little laugh.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:48.540
Weren't we?

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:49.420
Don't touch her!

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:54.750
Let's go.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.290
Wait.

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.330
Wait, Daisy!

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:01.710
Don't...

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.420
Please don't leave me!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.920
I'm sorry!

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.250
I'm sorry, Beatrice.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.380
He can't control himself.

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.420
He used to be an expert steam engineer.

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:35.040
But he got hurt in an accident, and it changed him.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.290
Oh, his right hand...

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:41.080
He hates everyone around him, envies them.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:45.210
He blames all of his problems on everyone else.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.290
Why're ya looking at me like that!

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.130
If you have something to say, then say it!

00:10:50.460 --> 00:10:52.880
You think I'm a laughingstock, too!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:56.790
What's wrong?
Why don't you run out on me like SHE did?!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.580
That's dreadful!

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:00.420
He's a weak man.

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:03.960
He would beat me within an inch of my life,
then he'd always...

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:09.250
I'm sorry, Daisy. I'm so sorry.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.330
I couldn't take it anymore, so I ran away.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:15.540
To what is now the Commonwealth.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.250
The Revolution came that same day.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:21.380
So you could never go back.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:23.080
Pretty much.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.420
It was a relief, actually.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:28.790
I figured I'd never have to see him again.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.830
Mum ran out on us both, so I'm grateful
that he didn't abandon me, too, but...

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:37.040
Why are you telling me all this?

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:40.380
I thought spies didn't reveal their histories.

00:11:40.630 --> 00:11:42.500
That's definitely true of Ange.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.670
I think...

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:46.710
I'm weaker than she is.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.500
That, and...

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.460
...I thought if anyone would understand, you would.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.130
Sorry.

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:01.040
Well, if that's how you're going to talk, Miss Dorothy,

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:05.170
this isn't just a cover anymore... we're real friends now!

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:08.580
What? Did I say anything to imply that?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.710
Do you really believe that?

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.790
That you can change the world?

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:21.500
Yes.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.880
But even if you could become Queen...

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:27.420
I want to stop having to hide our relationship, Charlotte.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.250
So do I!

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.290
But we're not the only ones who feel this way.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:39.250
Parents, siblings, lovers, friends...

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:42.880
So many people have been torn apart by that Wall.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:46.540
One day, their voices will all come together.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:49.000
Like a giant wave.

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.210
And you're going to wait for it?

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.960
I've waited ten years already.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:58.420
Besides, it won't be like those ten years anymore.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.380
You're not alone anymore.

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:09.130
I can't believe you're already drunk.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:12.040
Ugh, you're getting old.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:15.330
Eh, shut up! I'm still...

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.330
Come on, we're here!

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:34.250
Well? Brings back memories, don't it?

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.380
Come on in, Beatrice.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:50.420
He won't be waking any time soon.

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:51.330
All right.

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:56.040
He must have some way
to contact the Duke of Normandy.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.790
It should be in here somewhere.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:13:59.580
I'll help you look.

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:13.580
This is...

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:18.960
The Moon is beautiful.

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:21.380
And we fell...

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:24.380
Like he hasn't a care in the world.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.710
Owww...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.210
Are you all right?

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.540
Dorothy?

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.420
I'm Daisy.

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:40.960
Oh, right. Of course.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:43.540
You know Mum would never come back here.

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:45.380
Want some water?

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:48.670
No, I'd rather be drunk, thanks.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.920
Anyway, we need to talk.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:54.210
I'm not interested in a walk
down our rubbish memory lane.

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:55.920
It's about money.

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.920
A body's gonna show up at the morgue.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.670
One with a cross carved into the palm of his hand.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.630
And there's a note hidden in his tooth.

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:06.790
What's the point of that?

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:07.960
It doesn't matter.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:13.330
The important thing is that
if we take it to a certain person, we'll be rich.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:15.880
Got it, Daisy?

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.920
A cross on the palm of his hand.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:21.130
When you find the body, you tell me straightaway.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:25.250
All right, Dad. I got it.

00:15:26.540 --> 00:15:29.040
Have you found the cipher?

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:31.460
We are currently searching for the body.

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:34.170
I've made arrangements at the morgue.

00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.170
A scavenger, eh?

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:38.000
Can you trust him?

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:40.460
The man has debts to pay.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:46.460
Those motivated by money
are always the most predictable.

00:15:51.170 --> 00:15:52.670
W-wait, please!

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.170
I'll be getting the money soon, all of it!

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:57.380
Then I swear I'll pay you back!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.630
And you expect me to believe that?

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:00.710
Oh, I know!

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:04.210
If YOU can't pay, maybe we'll ask
your daughter to get us the money.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.420
She really is quite a beauty.

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.460
Say the word, and I could consider your loan repaid.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:25.040
That's...!

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:36.420
What happened to your face?

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.210
N-nothing. Get back to work!

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:43.710
I bet it was just another drunken brawl anyway!

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:45.170
Miss Dorothy!

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:14.380
So that's the cipher?

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:16.500
Yes. I'm going to copy it.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:19.130
We can't just take it with us?

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.880
We don't want the Duke of Normandy to find out.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:23.210
Besides...

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.630
This will help my dad.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:30.630
Never mind. Let's hurry.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:31.790
Right.

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:35.920
Not him, either.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.000
Owww. Dammit.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.290
If I just had the money, I'd kiss this place goodbye.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.250
Dad!

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.750
What? What do you want?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:46.920
I found it!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.250
Here.

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:53.500
You did it, Daisy!

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.210
That's my girl!

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:58.960
Ugh, don't get carried away.

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:00.830
Get away from me, you reek of booze.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.170
Don't say that!

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:04.630
You'll be drinking with me tonight! To celebrate!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:05.630
Uh, wait!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:06.500
Dad!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:08.750
Oh, pardon me.

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.130
Wait for me at the pub on Ghost Street!

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:12.330
Bring your friend!

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:14.880
I'm kissing this rubbish life goodbye!

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:20.210
Money, money! I'm rich!

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.420
I'm here, my lovely.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.080
Do you have it?

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.460
I wouldn't be here if I didn't.

00:18:40.040 --> 00:18:41.710
Let me make sure.

00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.880
Ah-ah-ah, terms first.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:47.420
You need it, don't you?

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.630
So let's see a little more money in return, eh?

00:18:52.460 --> 00:18:54.670
The pub on Ghost Street?

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:57.710
Yeah. Dad told me to meet him there.

00:18:57.880 --> 00:18:59.330
That's wonderful.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:02.880
You patched things up with your father.

00:19:02.880 --> 00:19:04.580
Oh, I don't know about that.

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:05.630
What's this?

00:19:05.920 --> 00:19:08.920
Goodness gracious, she came with a bonus!

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:16.420
I didn't think he'd give me TWO.
What surprisingly good service.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:18.380
What are you talking about?

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.000
Oh, no, didn't he tell you?

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:23.830
Your father owes me a lot of money.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.710
She's a nice bit of skirt, too.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:28.210
That'll cover interest and then some.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:30.540
I don't follow.

00:19:30.960 --> 00:19:35.630
It's only logical that the daughter
would shoulder her father's debt, isn't it?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.880
Don't hate me. Hate the fact
that you had that louse for a father.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:43.670
Wait for me at the pub on Ghost Street!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:46.170
I'm kissing this rubbish life goodbye!

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:48.380
Dad...

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:53.750
You just have to face facts.

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:55.500
And you, too, Little Lady.

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:00.920
Wench!

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:06.040
Hey, stop! What is wrong with you, woman?!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:10.500
Sorry, but I am beyond furious right now.

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:13.040
I can't hold myself back!

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.540
What are you doing?

00:20:14.540 --> 00:20:16.250
Get up and show her what for!

00:20:17.460 --> 00:20:17.960
Beatrice!

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:18.920
G-got it!

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:26.830
Damn you!

00:20:32.880 --> 00:20:35.500
Why did I ever think SHE was a looker?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:36.960
You she-devil!

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.880
Ow, that hurt!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:42.670
No, stop! Stop!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:47.670
Y-you came here alone, so I assumed
he'd given his seal of approval!

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:49.630
What do you mean?

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:53.290
I told him to give us his daughter to pay off his loan.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.580
And he...

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:57.330
Soon! I'm getting a lot of money soon!

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.170
Let go of me!

00:20:58.170 --> 00:20:59.750
I swear I'll pay you back!

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:03.330
So please, not my daughter! Anything but that!

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:08.830
We hit him, we kicked him, but that's all he would say!
Like a broken record.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:11.580
Dad...

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.630
Took quite a lot of work getting this.

00:21:14.630 --> 00:21:18.380
Searching corpses with my daughter, day in and day out.

00:21:18.500 --> 00:21:19.460
Your daughter?

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:20.750
That's right.

00:21:20.750 --> 00:21:23.580
That's why I want you to pay both of us.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.330
I wouldn't recommend getting too greedy.

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:29.170
She's a beautiful girl.

00:21:29.290 --> 00:21:30.920
I'm gonna buy her some clothes,

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:32.830
and we'll walk around town together.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:36.960
I'll say, "Look at that? Ain't she a beauty?"
to everyone we meet.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:39.250
Because it's a miracle.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:43.210
I never thought I'd see her again, but there she was.

00:21:43.460 --> 00:21:46.670
So we need some funds to start over.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:50.080
I'm gonna say goodbye to this rubbish life,

00:21:50.080 --> 00:21:52.250
and turn over a new leaf!

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:53.460
Really.

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:55.290
Then I'll help you.

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:00.540
I'll put an end to this "rubbish life" of yours.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:02.380
No, I...!

00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:12.290
What a busy pub!

00:22:12.460 --> 00:22:14.960
There aren't any other good pubs in the area.

00:22:15.630 --> 00:22:18.040
And they serve a pretty decent stout, if nothing else.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:21.960
I'll excuse myself as soon as your father gets here.

00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:23.920
Assuming he ever does.

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:26.460
He's not exactly the type to keep his promises.

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:30.630
But he really does care about you.

00:22:30.630 --> 00:22:32.210
Oh, stop it.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:37.170
If he had been even a little more decent a human being,
I wouldn't have run away.

00:22:37.630 --> 00:22:39.630
And you wouldn't have become a spy?

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:43.000
I might be hawking bread for a baker somewhere.

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:47.540
Then I have your father to thank
that I got to meet you, Miss Dorothy.

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:51.540
Even if he is the weakest,
most worthless father of all time.

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:56.000
He was a good dad, back when he was still an engineer.

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:58.750
He used to sing me to sleep.

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:02.750
Dad and I both loved that song.

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.580
The Moon is beautiful

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:08.290
And we fell in love

00:23:08.290 --> 00:23:09.380
Come on, stop it!
And we fell in love

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:10.500
And we fell in love

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:12.790
On just a dazzling summer's night

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:14.750
That's pretty good, Miss!
On just a dazzling summer's night

00:23:14.750 --> 00:23:15.630
Nice singing!
On just a dazzling summer's night

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:18.290
On just a dazzling summer's night

00:23:18.580 --> 00:23:26.500
We dance the light steps of a merry melody

00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:29.130
Laughing as we go

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:34.540
Exchanging kiss after kiss

00:23:34.670 --> 00:23:42.210
So on nights when the moon is beautiful, remember

00:23:42.710 --> 00:23:50.250
Although we're so far apart now

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:51.460
You are dearer to me than anything in the world

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:52.920
You're late.
You are dearer to me than anything in the world

00:23:52.920 --> 00:23:54.330
Dad.
You are dearer to me than anything in the world

00:23:54.330 --> 00:23:58.380
You are dearer to me than anything in the world

00:23:58.670 --> 00:24:02.250
And I am here

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:07.290
Singing
